# Context allowlist for docker/swarm/Dockerfile (BuildKit reads the ignore file
# named after the Dockerfile). Everything is excluded unless listed here, so
# keypairs, runtime state, the Node stack, and the Flask app never enter the
# build context.
*
!cli/
!worker/
!backend/app/__init__.py
!backend/app/config.py
!backend/app/protocol/
!backend/app/utils/llm_client.py
!docker/swarm/pyproject.toml
!docker/swarm/uv.lock
# The zkVM branch canonicalization guest and the host that verifies it. The shared
# reducer crate is a path dependency of both, so both directories have to enter.
!protocol/zkvm-reducer/
!protocol/bonsol-aggregate-reducer/
# The one declaration of the RISC Zero component versions and of where the guest is
# compiled, and the two scripts that read it. Every image that builds the guest goes
# through them, so the Dockerfile holds none of those values itself.
!protocol/risc0-toolchain.env
!scripts/install-risc0-toolchain.sh
!scripts/build-zkvm-guest.sh
# Named in full rather than by a `**/target` glob: `bonsol build` leaves a root-owned
# `target/` in the guest crates, the context sender fails on it with "permission
# denied", and the glob did not exclude it at this depth. Nothing in `target/` belongs
# in an image anyway; the stage builds its own.
protocol/zkvm-reducer/target
protocol/bonsol-aggregate-reducer/target
# Never needed inside an image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/tests/
**/target
cli/uv.lock
